# 📜 Changelog

All notable changes to MadiLang are documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0/).

---

## 🚀 [v0.5.2] — PyPI Publication — 2026-07-04

> 📦 **"Sovereignty is now a pip install away."**

Official PyPI publication of MadiLang, making it available for easy installation across all Python environments.

### 🌟 Highlights
- 📦 **Official PyPI Publication**: MadiLang is now available via `pip install madilang`# 📜 Changelog
- ✅ All v0.5.0 features included (Python/FastAPI, `madi doctor`, Hybrid Adapter, Modular CLI)

---

## 🚀 [v0.5.0] — Multi-Target Sovereignty & Diagnostics — 2026-06-21

> 🐍 **"Sovereignty speaks every language."**
> 🩺 **"Trust is verified, not assumed."**

This release transforms MadiLang from a single-target tool into a **multi-target sovereign platform**. With Python/FastAPI support, instant environment diagnostics, and a modular CLI architecture, MadiLang now delivers production-ready backends across ecosystems while maintaining cryptographic proof of origin.

### 🌟 Highlights

- 🐍 **Python/FastAPI Generator**: Full async backend generation with Pydantic models, automatic validation, and Uvicorn server setup.
- 🩺 **`madi doctor` Command**: Comprehensive environment diagnostics checking Python, Node.js, npm, network, secrets, and permissions.
- 🛡️ **Sovereign Hybrid Adapter**: Intelligent database fallback ensuring generated code runs everywhere without configuration hell.
- 🏗️ **Modular CLI Architecture**: Lazy-loaded command modules for faster startup and cleaner codebase.
- ✅ **10/10 CI Checks**: All tests passing across Python 3.8–3.13 including mobile validation.
- 📱 **Mobile-First Verified**: Full development cycle tested on Termux/Android.

---

### ✨ Added

#### 🐍 Python/FastAPI Generator
- `madilang/generators/python/generator.py`: Complete FastAPI code generator with async handlers. - Pydantic model generation 
from entity definitions with type mapping. - Automatic input validation via Pydantic schemas. - Uvicorn server setup with 
configurable port. - `requirements.txt` generation with FastAPI, Uvicorn, and Pydantic dependencies. All notable changes to 
MadiLang are documented in this file. - Hybrid database adapter with in-memory mock fallback. - Sovereign signature embedding 
in Python comment syntax. - Runtime verification helper (`__verify_madi_signature__`). The format is based on [Keep a 
Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/), and this project adheres to [Semantic 
Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0/).

